York Engineering Competition (YEC)
Official Qualification Policy & Rules for OEC Progression
Overview
To ensure that York University is represented by the most dedicated, engaged, and qualified teams at the Ontario Engineering Competition (OEC), the YEC Organizing Committee has established a standardized qualification framework. Competitors seeking to secure a spot to represent York University at OEC must satisfy all eligibility criteria outlined below.
Qualification Criteria
Criteria 1: Engineering Major Requirement (Mandatory)
* Requirement: All competitors advancing to OEC MUST be currently enrolled in an Engineering degree program/major at York University.
* Details: Non-engineering majors are strictly ineligible to represent York University at OEC, regardless of team performance or event participation.
Criteria 2: Team Roster & Size Requirements
* Requirement: The number of members in a team must match EXACTLY the team size specified in the competition-specific handbook.
* Details: If your team does not meet the exact required head count, reach out to the YEC Organizers. The YEC team will assist in matching or rearranging competitors to ensure full compliance with the handbook rules.
Criteria 3: Unanimous Judge Panel Approval PER COMPETITION 
* Requirement: A team's placement and progression to OEC must be unanimously agreed upon by the official judging panel.
* Details: Beyond overall points, every member of the judging panel must concur that the team's project, presentation, and design demonstrate the calibre required to represent York University at OEC.
Criteria 4: Mandatory Event Engagement (Passport Stamps)
* Requirement: Competitors must collect all required stamps from tablers and/or workshops in their official YEC Event Passport.
* Important Note: Please keep your YEC Event Passport safe at all times, as lost passports cannot be replaced or re-stamped and are required to confirm eligibility.
Criteria 5: Judge Scoring Threshold
* Requirement: Competitors must meet or exceed the required scoring threshold evaluated by the judging panel.
* Details: Performance will be evaluated based on official competition rubrics, including technical design, feasibility, and presentation quality.
Selection Process
* Qualification spots for OEC are limited.
* Candidates who satisfy all qualification criteria will be selected based on their performance and unanimous judge panel endorsement.
* In order to score extra points, competitors are NOT MANDATED but  incentivised to attend the Semi Annual General Meeting hosted by Lassonde Engineering Society (LES) which will be held on Friday, November 13th, 2026. Registration desk will be set BRG125 where competitors can register for extra YEC points. 


For questions or clarifications regarding these rules, please contact the yec@lasengsoc.com (YEC Vice Chair of Competition).